      en: 'Jasimuddin (1903–1976), remembered as the Polli Kobi or poet of rural Bengal, wrote about village people, landscapes and sorrows in works such as "Nakshi Kanthar Math", "Sojan Badiyar Ghat" and the poem "Kabar". His family home at Ambikapur, on the bank of the Kumar river just outside Faridpur town, is now a memorial museum.\n\nVisitors can walk through the traditional tin-roofed house and see photographs, personal belongings and copies of manuscripts. The poet is buried beside the house, by his wish under a pomegranate tree, echoing his famous poem about a grave. The house of "Asmani", the poor girl from another of his poems, is close by.\n\nThe setting is quiet for most of the year, but in January the Jasim Mela, held around his birthday, fills the area with stalls, folk music and visitors.',
