      en: 'A short ride from Faridpur town, Dholar Mor on the bank of the Padma is where townspeople come to spend their afternoons. From the bank the river opens out into a vast sheet of water, with sandbars on the horizon and fishing boats drifting past, and the breeze is a welcome escape from the heat of town.\n\nAs the afternoon wears on, families, friends and students gather, and stalls selling jhalmuri, fuchka and tea do brisk business. At sunset the sky and the water turn red and orange together, which is the moment most people wait for.\n\nThe river changes with the seasons: in the monsoon it runs fast, brown and very wide, while in winter the water drops and broad sandbars emerge. The riverbank can erode, so the exact viewing spot may shift from year to year.',
