      en: 'Scattered through the village of Ulpur in Gopalganj Sadar are a number of old buildings from the zamindari era. Local accounts say a landowning family built these houses, temples and bathing ghats during British rule; after Partition many were abandoned, while a few are now used by local offices or residents.\n\nArched windows, crumbling cornices, banyan roots splitting the brickwork and silent ponds give Ulpur a melancholy beauty. There is no formal site, ticket counter or signage — you simply wander the village lanes and come upon the buildings one after another.\n\nBecause it is so little known, Ulpur has become a quiet favourite of photographers looking for texture and atmosphere. The soft light of a winter morning brings out the colours of the old walls best, and the village is pleasantly calm at that hour.',
