      en: 'Charmuguria, on the Arial Khan river just outside Madaripur town, was a well-known river port for the jute trade in the British period. Boats and steamers brought jute in from the surrounding countryside, and from warehouses here it was shipped on to Calcutta and beyond. That boom is long over, but rows of old godowns and merchant buildings still hint at the busy days.\n\nToday Charmuguria is best known for its monkeys. Troops of them roam freely across the area — on market roofs, in the trees and along the lanes — and local people have lived alongside them for generations. Watching them move through the old bazar is the main attraction for most visitors.\n\nIt is a small, quirky stop rather than a full-day destination, easy to pair with Shakuni Lake. Mornings and late afternoons are the most comfortable and the monkeys are most active then.',
